<title>POLAND: Optimus seeks to assimilate 2.5 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Optimus seeks to assimilate 2.5 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish computer maker Optimus SA applied to the Warsaw bourse to assimilate the 2.5 million shares to cover its convertible bond issue, the company said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The shares, which were cleared for trade by the Polish Securities Commission last month, are to be exchanged for the firm's 300 five-year convertible bonds.</p>
<p>One convertible bond is exchangeable into 6,947 common shares at 38.76 zlotys a share before the bonds mature on June 20, 2001.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
